  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 2-5 where prices fell from ~74 to ~68); forecasts consistently overshoot the true outcome by 1.5x to 2x the actual drop magnitude.",
    "When sentiment is neutral or slightly negative (-0.25) following a price decline, the model fails to capture mean reversion spikes (e.g., Example 2-5), predicting a slow linear recovery while true outcomes show sharp V-shaped rebounds within 7-10 days.",
    "The model suffers from horizon-specific lag: it assumes a smooth monotonic trend but actual EU ETS prices exhibit high volatility with sudden reversals that occur before the forecasted turning point is reached.",
    "In volatile regimes (Example 2-5), the model's low-slope forecasts underestimate the amplitude of price swings, resulting in systematic under-prediction of both downside crashes and upside spikes relative to the true range."
  ]
}
